<%- include('partials/head') %>
<%
  const base = (publicUrl || 'https://your-novadesk') + '/api/v1';
  const tags = spec.tags.map(t => t.name);
  const ops = [];
  Object.entries(spec.paths).forEach(([path, methods]) => Object.entries(methods).forEach(([method, op]) => ops.push({ path, method: method.toUpperCase(), op })));
  const badge = { GET: 'success', POST: 'primary', PATCH: 'warning text-dark', DELETE: 'danger' };
  const typeOf = (s) => (s.enum ? s.enum.join(' | ') : (s.format ? s.type + ' (' + s.format + ')' : s.type)) + (s.nullable ? ', may be null' : '');
%>
<div class="container py-4" style="max-width: 980px;">
  <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center mb-3">
    <h3 class="mb-0"><i class="bi bi-braces text-primary me-2"></i>NovaDesk API</h3>
    <a href="/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Back to NovaDesk</a>
  </div>
  <p class="text-muted">Create and read incidents, service requests and configuration items from your own scripts and tools. JSON over HTTPS, one personal API key per integration. The machine-readable description is at <a href="<%= specPath %>"><%= specPath %></a> (OpenAPI 3).</p>

  <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body">
    <h5>Getting started</h5>
    <ol class="mb-2">
      <li>Open <a href="/profile/api-keys">your profile menu, API keys</a> and make a key. Choose <em>Read only</em> unless the integration must create or change records. The key is shown once.</li>
      <li>Send it with every request: <code>Authorization: Bearer ndk_…</code>.</li>
    </ol>
<pre class="border rounded p-3 small mb-2">curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $NOVADESK_KEY" <%= base %>/me

curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $NOVADESK_KEY" \
     "<%= base %>/incidents?status=open&amp;priority=1"

curl -X POST <%= base %>/incidents \
     -H "Authorization: Bearer $NOVADESK_KEY" \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     -H "Idempotency-Key: 3f1c0c1e-8a52-4e4e-9a31-0b5d5b1c1111" \
     -d '{"short_description": "Disk full on PRD-DB-01", "impact": 2, "urgency": 1}'

curl -X PATCH <%= base %>/incidents/42 \
     -H "Authorization: Bearer $NOVADESK_KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     -d '{"status": "on_hold"}'</pre>
    <p class="small text-muted mb-0">A key acts as the person who made it, with their role: an end user sees and creates only their own incidents and requests; agents and administrators see everything. A key stops working when it expires, is revoked, or its owner is turned off. Keys are not subject to two-step verification, so treat them like passwords and use as little access as the job needs.</p>
  </div></div>

  <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body">
    <h5>Conventions</h5>
    <dl class="row small mb-0">
      <dt class="col-sm-3">Format</dt><dd class="col-sm-9">Requests with a body use <code>Content-Type: application/json</code> (up to 256 KB). Dates and times in answers are ISO 8601 in UTC. Fields you send that the API does not know are refused, so a typo fails loudly.</dd>
      <dt class="col-sm-3">Lists</dt><dd class="col-sm-9">Newest first. <code>page</code> (from 1) and <code>per_page</code> (1 to 200, default 50). The answer is <code>{ "data": [...], "page", "per_page", "total" }</code>, and the total is also in <code>X-Total-Count</code>.</dd>
      <dt class="col-sm-3">Creating</dt><dd class="col-sm-9">Answers <code>201</code> with the new record and a <code>Location</code> header.</dd>
      <dt class="col-sm-3">Changing</dt><dd class="col-sm-9"><code>PATCH</code> takes only the fields to change; <code>null</code> clears a field that allows it. A change goes through the same rules as one made in the browser: priorities and SLA clocks are recalculated, the activity log is written and the right people are emailed.</dd>
      <dt class="col-sm-3">Safe retries</dt><dd class="col-sm-9">Add an <code>Idempotency-Key</code> header (any unique string, such as a UUID) to a <code>POST</code>. Repeating the same request with the same key within 24 hours returns the first answer (with <code>Idempotent-Replay: true</code>) and creates nothing new. Using the key for a different request is refused with <code>422</code>.</dd>
      <dt class="col-sm-3">Errors</dt><dd class="col-sm-9"><code>{ "error": { "code", "message", "details": [{ "field", "message" }] } }</code> with the matching HTTP status: 400 invalid request, 401 no valid key, 403 not allowed (a read-only key, or your role), 404 not found, 409 an identical request is still running, 413 body too large, 415 not JSON, 422 a field refers to something that does not exist, 429 too many requests.</dd>
      <dt class="col-sm-3">Rate limits</dt><dd class="col-sm-9"><% if (limits.apiPerMinute) { %><%= limits.apiPerMinute %> reads and <%= limits.apiWritePerMinute %> writes per key per minute<% } else { %>No per-key limit is set<% } %>; every answer carries <code>X-RateLimit-Limit</code>, <code>X-RateLimit-Remaining</code> and <code>X-RateLimit-Reset</code> (seconds). Over the limit you get <code>429</code> and <code>Retry-After</code>. An address is also limited as a whole, and repeated bad keys from one address are blocked for a while.</dd>
    </dl>
  </div></div>

  <h5 class="mb-3">Endpoints</h5>
  <% tags.forEach(tag => { %>
  <h6 class="text-uppercase text-muted mt-4 mb-2" style="letter-spacing:.06em;"><%= tag %></h6>
  <% ops.filter(o => o.op.tags[0] === tag).forEach(o => { %>
  <div class="card mb-2"><div class="card-body py-2">
    <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
      <span class="badge bg-<%= badge[o.method] || 'secondary' %>" style="min-width:3.8em;"><%= o.method %></span>
      <code class="fs-6">/api/v1<%= o.path %></code>
      <span class="ms-2"><%= o.op.summary %></span>
    </div>
    <% if (o.op.description) { %><p class="small text-muted mb-1 mt-1"><%= o.op.description %></p><% } %>
    <% const params = (o.op.parameters || []); if (params.length) { %>
    <table class="table table-sm small mb-1 mt-2"><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>In</th><th>Values</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <% params.forEach(p => { %><tr><td><code><%= p.name %></code></td><td><%= p.in %></td><td><%= typeOf(p.schema) %></td><td class="text-muted"><%= p.description || '' %></td></tr><% }) %>
    </tbody></table>
    <% } %>
    <% if (o.op.requestBody) { const sch = o.op.requestBody.content['application/json'].schema; %>
    <table class="table table-sm small mb-1 mt-2"><thead><tr><th>Body field</th><th>Required</th><th>Values</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <% Object.entries(sch.properties).forEach(([name, s]) => { %><tr><td><code><%= name %></code></td><td><%= sch.required.includes(name) ? 'yes' : '' %></td><td><%= typeOf(s) %></td><td class="text-muted"><%= s.description || '' %></td></tr><% }) %>
    </tbody></table>
    <% } %>
    <div class="small text-muted mt-1">Answer: <code><%= Object.values(o.op.responses)[0].content['application/json'].schema.$ref.split('/').pop() %></code><%= o.op.responses[403] ? ' · needs ' + (o.method === 'GET' ? 'a role that may see it' : 'a write key') : '' %></div>
  </div></div>
  <% }) %>
  <% }) %>

  <h5 class="mt-5 mb-3" id="webhooks">Webhooks</h5>
  <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body">
    <p>Instead of asking NovaDesk what changed, let NovaDesk tell you. An administrator adds a webhook under <em>Webhooks</em> in the user menu: an address, the events wanted, and NovaDesk makes a signing secret. From then on every matching event is sent to that address as an HTTP <code>POST</code> with a JSON body.</p>
    <h6>Events</h6>
    <p class="small mb-2">For incidents, changes, problems, service requests, configuration items (<code>ci</code>) and knowledge articles: <code>&lt;record&gt;.created</code>, <code>&lt;record&gt;.updated</code> (any other change to the record; the SLA clock bookkeeping and article view counts do not count) and <code>&lt;record&gt;.status_changed</code> (with the previous status); for incidents, changes and problems also <code>&lt;record&gt;.commented</code>. Internal work notes on incidents are never sent. Events are recorded by the database itself, so changes made through the pages, the API, the integrations and the decommission automation all produce them. Moving a record to another status sends <code>status_changed</code> only, not also <code>updated</code>. A test button sends <code>ping</code>.</p>
    <h6>What you receive</h6>
<pre class="border rounded p-3 small">POST /your/endpoint
Content-Type: application/json
User-Agent: NovaDesk-Webhooks/1
X-NovaDesk-Event: incident.status_changed
X-NovaDesk-Event-Id: evt_3b1f6a52-...        (the same for every retry of this event)
X-NovaDesk-Delivery: 118
X-NovaDesk-Signature: t=1798761600,v1=5257a869e7ecebeda32affa62cdca3fa51cad7e77a0e56ff536d0ce8e108d8bd

{
  "id": "evt_3b1f6a52-...",
  "type": "incident.status_changed",
  "created_at": "2026-12-01T10:15:00Z",
  "data": { "incident": { "id": 42, "number": "INC0000042", "status": "on_hold", ... } },
  "previous": { "status": "in_progress" }
}</pre>
    <p class="small">The record is shown exactly as the REST API shows it (see the endpoints above), as it was right after the change that caused the event (not as it is by the time the call arrives, so a quick series of changes each shows its own state). <code>commented</code> events carry a <code>comment</code> object as well.</p>
    <h6>Checking a call is genuine</h6>
    <p class="small mb-2">The signature is the hex HMAC-SHA256, with your secret as the key, of the timestamp, a dot and the raw body: <code>HMAC(secret, "&lt;t&gt;." + body)</code>. Compare it in constant time and refuse a timestamp more than five minutes old.</p>
<pre class="border rounded p-3 small">// Node.js
const crypto = require('crypto');
function genuine(secret, header, rawBody) {
  const m = /^t=(\d+),v1=([0-9a-f]{64})$/.exec(header || '');
  if (!m || Math.abs(Date.now() / 1000 - Number(m[1])) > 300) return false;
  const expected = crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret).update(m[1] + '.' + rawBody).digest();
  return crypto.timingSafeEqual(expected, Buffer.from(m[2], 'hex'));
}

# Python
import hmac, hashlib, re, time
def genuine(secret: str, header: str, raw_body: bytes) -> bool:
    m = re.fullmatch(r"t=(\d+),v1=([0-9a-f]{64})", header or "")
    if not m or abs(time.time() - int(m[1])) > 300:
        return False
    expected = hmac.new(secret.encode(), m[1].encode() + b"." + raw_body, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()
    return hmac.compare_digest(expected, m[2])</pre>
    <h6>Delivery rules</h6>
    <ul class="small mb-0">
      <li>Answer with any <code>2xx</code> within 10 seconds. Anything else, a timeout or a refused connection is a failure; redirects are not followed.</li>
      <li>A failed delivery is tried again after 1 minute, 5 minutes, 30 minutes, 2 hours and 6 hours, then given up (six tries). The administrator sees every try, can look at what was sent, and can retry by hand.</li>
      <li>A receiver whose last 10 deliveries all failed is switched off, so it is not called for ever.</li>
      <li>A retry carries the same <code>X-NovaDesk-Event-Id</code>: use it to ignore a repeat. Order is not guaranteed; use <code>updated_at</code> in the record.</li>
      <li>Only <code>https://</code> addresses that resolve to public addresses are accepted (so a webhook cannot be aimed at a server's own network). An administrator can allow private addresses and plain http for an internal receiver with <code>WEBHOOK_ALLOW_PRIVATE=true</code>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div></div>

  <p class="small text-muted mt-4">Changes, approvals and the decommission workflow are read-only here: approving, rejecting and cancelling follow their own rules in the NovaDesk pages.</p>
</div>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
